{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification encodes a conservative exploration supervisor: it enables random_walk in clear states, short forward progress via move_forward, and explicit, directed recovery turns when obstacles are detected. Obstacle recovery states allow only a single, safe turn action, and return to exploration as soon as the path is clear. Full_rotate is reserved for the rare case of being blocked on all sides.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect open-loop actuation and sensor events.",
    "Specification automaton encodes a compact, deterministic supervisor: random_walk and move_forward alternate in clear states, obstacle events force explicit turn recovery, and recovery states only allow a single safe action before returning to exploration."
